:Namespace test_Sessions
⍝ Session tests for Jarvis
⍝ Usage:
⍝   From the shell (repository root):  dyalogscript Tests/Sessions/run.apls
⍝   From an APL session with #.Jarvis loaded:  #.test_Sessions.Run
⍝ Run returns a vector of failure messages; empty means every test passed.
⍝ Each test starts its own Jarvis on its own port and drives it with a raw Conga client (Jarvis's own LDRC),
⍝ sending complete HTTP requests with "Connection: close" so the whole response can be read back.
⍝ Ports: BasePort+1, BasePort+2, ... (8491 and up by default). Set BasePort before Run, or JARVIS_TEST_PORT for run.apls.

    (⎕IO ⎕ML)←1 1
    CRLF←⎕UCS 13 10
    BasePort←8490
    Verbose←1

    TJarvisSource←':Class TJarvis: #.Jarvis' ':Field Public Logged←⍬' '∇ {msg}←{level}Log msg' ':Access public override' 'Logged,←⊂,⍕msg' '∇' ':EndClass'

    ∇ r←Run;tests;t;res
      :Access public
      r←⍬
      :If 9≠#.⎕NC'Jarvis'
          →0⊣r←,⊂'#.Jarvis is not loaded'
      :EndIf
      ⎕FIX TJarvisSource
      tests←{⍵/⍨'test_'∘≡¨5↑¨⍵}⎕NL ¯3
      PortsUsed←0
      :For t :In tests
          App←MakeApp
          (Servers Clients)←⍬ ⍬
          :Trap 0
              res←⍎t
          :Else
              res←,⊂'errored: ',⊃⎕DMX.DM
          :EndTrap
          StopAll
          r,←(⊂t,': '),¨res
          :If Verbose
              ⎕←t,': ',(1+0∊⍴res)⊃('FAILED (',(⍕≢res),')')'passed'
              ⎕←⍪res
          :EndIf
      :EndFor
    ∇

⍝ ─── the application code (CodeLocation) used by the tests ─────────────────────────

    ∇ app←MakeApp
      app←⎕NS''
      app.⎕FX'r←ping p' 'r←''pong'''                                   ⍝ a non-session endpoint
      app.⎕FX'r←req count p' 'req.Session.n+←1' 'r←req.Session.n'       ⍝ per-session counter (req as ⍺)
      app.⎕FX'r←InitSession req' 'req.Session.n←0' 'r←0'               ⍝ SessionInitFn
      app.⎕FX'r←BadInit req' 'r←1'                                      ⍝ SessionInitFn that fails
    ∇

⍝ ─── helpers ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    Expect←{⍺:0⍴⊂'' ⋄ ,⊂⍵}
    Contains←{∨/⍺⍷⍵}
    Match←{(,⍺)≡,⍵}

    ∇ j←NewServer dummy
      j←⎕NEW TJarvis
      j.Port←BasePort+PortsUsed←PortsUsed+1
      j.CodeLocation←App
      j.Paradigm←'JSON'
      j.DYALOG_JARVIS_THREAD←'debug'
      j.WaitTimeout←5000
      Servers,←j
    ∇

    ∇ StopAll;j;c
      :For j :In Servers
          :Trap 0 ⋄ {}j.Stop ⋄ {}j.LDRC.Close j.ServerName ⋄ :EndTrap
      :EndFor
      :For c :In Clients
          :Trap 0 ⋄ {}#.Jarvis.LDRC.Close c ⋄ :EndTrap
      :EndFor
      (Servers Clients)←⍬ ⍬
    ∇

    ∇ c←j SendRaw text;rc
      (rc c)←2↑j.LDRC.Clt'' 'localhost'j.Port'Text'
      'Could not connect'⎕SIGNAL 11/⍨rc≠0
      Clients,←⊂c
      {}j.LDRC.Send c text
    ∇

    ∇ (status headers body)←j Do args;method;path;headers;body;req;c
    ⍝ args: method path [headers [body]]; headers is a vector of (name value) pairs
      (method path headers body)←4↑args,(≢args)↓'' '' ⍬ ''
      req←method,' ',path,' HTTP/1.1',CRLF,'Host: localhost',CRLF,'Connection: close',CRLF
      req,←∊{⍺,': ',⍵,CRLF}/¨headers
      req,←(method≢'GET')/'Content-Length: ',(⍕≢body),CRLF
      req,←CRLF,body
      c←j SendRaw req
      (status headers body)←ParseResponse j ReadAll(c 4000)
    ∇

    ∇ data←j ReadAll(c ms);end;w;rc;evt
      data←'' ⋄ end←ms+⎕AI[3]
      :While ⎕AI[3]<end
          w←4↑(j.LDRC.Wait c 200),4⍴⊂''
          (rc evt)←w[1 3]
          :If rc=0
              :If (⊂evt)∊'Block' 'BlockLast' ⋄ data,←4⊃w ⋄ :EndIf
              :If (⊂evt)∊'BlockLast' 'Closed' 'Error' ⋄ :Leave ⋄ :EndIf
          :ElseIf rc≠100 ⋄ :Leave
          :EndIf
      :EndWhile
    ∇

    ∇ (status headers body)←ParseResponse data;i;head;lines
      status←0 ⋄ headers←0 2⍴⊂'' ⋄ body←''
      →0⍴⍨0∊⍴i←⍸(CRLF,CRLF)⍷data
      head←(¯1+⊃i)↑data
      body←(3+⊃i)↓data
      lines←{⍵~⎕UCS 13}¨(head≠⎕UCS 10)⊆head
      status←⊃(//)⎕VFI 2⊃' '(≠⊆⊢)⊃lines
      headers←↑{i←⍵⍳':' ⋄ (⎕C(i-1)↑⍵)({⍵↓⍨+/∧\' '=⍵}i↓⍵)}¨1↓lines
    ∇

    ∇ r←headers Header name
      r←(headers[;1]⍳⊂⎕C name)⊃headers[;2],⊂''
    ∇

    ∇ id←useCookie SessionIdOf headers
    ⍝ extract the session id from a response, from the header or the Set-Cookie, as appropriate
      :If useCookie
          id←2⊃('='(≠⊆⊢)⊃';'(≠⊆⊢)headers Header'set-cookie'),⊂''
      :Else
          id←headers Header'jarvis-sessionid'
      :EndIf
    ∇

    SendId←{⍺:('Cookie')('Jarvis-SessionID=',⍵) ⋄ ('Jarvis-SessionID')⍵}  ⍝ useCookie SendId id → a (name value) header pair

    JSONhdr←⊂'Content-Type' 'application/json'

⍝ ─── tests ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    ∇ r←test_NoSessions;j;status;headers;body
    ⍝ with SessionTimeout←0 (the default) no session id is issued
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer''
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      (status headers body)←j Do'POST' '/ping'JSONhdr'1'
      r,←(status=200)Expect'status ',⍕status
      r,←(0∊⍴headers Header'jarvis-sessionid')Expect'no session header should be sent when sessions are off'
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_SessionCreated;j;status;headers;body
    ⍝ enabling sessions issues a session id, and SessionInitFn initialises the session
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer''
      j.(SessionTimeout SessionInitFn)←30 'InitSession'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      (status headers body)←j Do'POST' '/count'JSONhdr'1'
      r,←(status=200)Expect'status ',⍕status
      r,←(~0∊⍴0 SessionIdOf headers)Expect'a session id should be issued'
      r,←('1'Match body)Expect'SessionInitFn should set n←0 so the first count is 1; got ',body
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_SessionPersists;j;h1;h2;h3;id;b1;b2;b3;s
    ⍝ returning the session id keeps the same session state; omitting it starts a new session
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer''
      j.(SessionTimeout SessionInitFn)←30 'InitSession'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      (s h1 b1)←j Do'POST' '/count'JSONhdr'1'
      id←0 SessionIdOf h1
      r,←('1'Match b1)Expect'first count ',b1
      (s h2 b2)←j Do'POST' '/count'(JSONhdr,⊂0 SendId id)'1'
      r,←('2'Match b2)Expect'second count with the same session should be 2; got ',b2
      (s h3 b3)←j Do'POST' '/count'JSONhdr'1'
      r,←('1'Match b3)Expect'a request without the session id should start a new session (count 1); got ',b3
      r,←(id≢0 SessionIdOf h3)Expect'the new session should have a different id'
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_SessionCookie;j;h1;h2;id;b1;b2;s
    ⍝ with SessionUseCookie the id travels in a Set-Cookie / Cookie
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer''
      j.(SessionTimeout SessionUseCookie SessionInitFn)←30 1 'InitSession'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      (s h1 b1)←j Do'POST' '/count'JSONhdr'1'
      id←1 SessionIdOf h1
      r,←(~0∊⍴id)Expect'a session cookie should be set; Set-Cookie was ',h1 Header'set-cookie'
      r,←('1'Match b1)Expect'first count ',b1
      (s h2 b2)←j Do'POST' '/count'(JSONhdr,⊂1 SendId id)'1'
      r,←('2'Match b2)Expect'second count with the session cookie should be 2; got ',b2
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_CustomHeader;j;h1;h2;id;b2;s
    ⍝ SessionIdHeader names the header that carries the id
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer''
      j.(SessionTimeout SessionInitFn SessionIdHeader)←30 'InitSession' 'X-My-Session'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      (s h1 b1)←j Do'POST' '/count'JSONhdr'1'
      id←h1 Header'x-my-session'
      r,←(~0∊⍴id)Expect'the custom session header should be present'
      (s h2 b2)←j Do'POST' '/count'(JSONhdr,⊂('X-My-Session')id)'1'
      r,←('2'Match b2)Expect'the session should resolve via the custom header (count 2); got ',b2
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_SessionInitFails;j;status;headers;body
    ⍝ a non-zero result from SessionInitFn fails the request with 500
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer''
      j.(SessionTimeout SessionInitFn)←30 'BadInit'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      (status headers body)←j Do'POST' '/ping'JSONhdr'1'
      r,←(status=500)Expect'a failing SessionInitFn should give 500; got ',⍕status
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_SessionTimeout;j;h1;h3;id;b1;b2;b3;s
    ⍝ a session that has been idle longer than SessionTimeout is discarded
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer''
      j.(SessionTimeout SessionPollingTime SessionInitFn)←0.05 0.02 'InitSession' ⍝ ~3s timeout, ~1.2s poll
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      (s h1 b1)←j Do'POST' '/count'JSONhdr'1'
      id←0 SessionIdOf h1
      (s h3 b2)←j Do'POST' '/count'(JSONhdr,⊂0 SendId id)'1'
      r,←('2'Match b2)Expect'before timeout the session should persist (count 2); got ',b2
      {}⎕DL 5 ⍝ wait for the session to time out
      (s h3 b3)←j Do'POST' '/count'(JSONhdr,⊂0 SendId id)'1'
      r,←('1'Match b3)Expect'after the timeout the session should be gone (count resets to 1); got ',b3
      r,←(id≢0 SessionIdOf h3)Expect'after the timeout a new session id should be issued'
    ∇

:EndNamespace
